# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nightly sweep, on the host that runs the central node.
#
# Not a GitHub `schedule:` trigger on purpose. A scheduled workflow only fires
# when the self-hosted runner is online, and GitHub delays scheduled runs
# under load - sometimes by tens of minutes, sometimes silently skipping them.
# For a job whose whole purpose is "notice that a regional server changed
# something while nobody was looking", that is the wrong reliability.
#
# Install (inspect the existing crontab first, never replace it):
#
#     crontab -l > /tmp/current.crontab
#     cat .github/workflows/nightly.crontab >> /tmp/current.crontab
#     crontab /tmp/current.crontab
#     crontab -l
#
# The push-triggered run in validate.yml stays as it is: this is the sweep,
# that is the gate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the repository is checked out on this host. Adjust both lines.
# `run pending` re-checks everything that is not currently healthy - blocked,
# unreachable, unhandled and anything newly declared - so a facility that fixed
# its metadata overnight is picked up without touching the registry, and a
# healthy federation costs nothing.

# m  h  dom mon dow  command
  17 2  *   *   *    cd /srv/emso-validation-gate && git pull --ff-only --quiet && ./gate.py run pending --trigger schedule >> /var/log/emso-gate.log 2>&1

# A full re-validation once a week, so a dataset that has been quietly passing
# for months is still re-checked against the current specifications.
  17 3  *   *   0    cd /srv/emso-validation-gate && ./gate.py run all --trigger schedule >> /var/log/emso-gate.log 2>&1

# Without the engine installed on the host, swap ./gate.py for ./gate.sh and
# these become `docker compose run --rm gate ...` instead.

# 02:17 rather than 02:00: every cron job on every host in the world fires on
# the hour, and the regional ERDDAPs being probed are on those hosts.
